{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["Eleven days from Horev — Version A: Who is wise and will understand this? For the verse was written only because it is written above: וניסע מחורב ונלך את כל המדבר הגדול והנורא דרך הר האמורי ונבוא עד קדש ברנע — adjacent to the land of Israel. From Kadesh Barnea they sent the spies and they were delayed there forty years; therefore he explains as follows. When they set out from Horev to travel by way of Mount Seir, a direct route, they could have entered the land of Israel in eleven days, until Kadesh Barnea. But because they sinned, ונסב את הר שעיר ימים רבים, up to forty years, etc. And this is what is said above: וניסע מחורב וגו׳ ונבוא עד קדש ברנע — in a few days that contain only an eleven-day journey, but from Kadesh Barnea I sent spies and you were delayed forty years for your sin.\nVersion B: This is the truth of the matter, that he begins to tell that they were not delayed on the road except eleven days from Horev to Kadesh Barnea, and immediately they were ready to enter the land of Israel by the same route the spies went, as Moshe said to them: עלו זה בנגב ועליתם את ההר — and as is said at the end of the pericope: וישכימו בבקר ויעלו אל ראש ההר וגו׳. וירד העמלקי והכנעני היושב בהר ההוא ויכום וגו׳ — and also above: ותזדו ותעלו ההרה. All these verses prove that immediately, had they not sinned in the matter of the spies, they were close to entering the land of Israel right away." "Kadesh Barnea — it is the wilderness of Paran. And when they set out from Horev in the second year, on the twentieth of the month, as written in the pericope of Behaʿalotekha: ויסעו מהר ה׳ דרך שלשת ימים — and above it is written at the beginning of the pericope: ויהי בשנה השנית — and written after it: ויסעו בני ישראל למסעיהם על פי ה׳ ממדבר סיני וישכון הענן במדבר פארן — and afterwards he goes on to tell how they came to the wilderness of Paran, in the course of which: ויהי העם כמתאוננים — and והתאוו תאוה, on account of which the name of the place was called קברות התאוה. From there they came to Hazeroth, and there Miriam was stricken with leprosy, and they were delayed there seven days, and after that the people set out from Hazeroth until they came and encamped in the wilderness of Paran — and this is וישכן הענן במדבר פארן — that is stated above. And this is: אחד עשר יום מחורב — that they traveled by way of Mount Seir three days, as written: ויסעו מהר ה׳ דרך שלשת ימים — and seven days during which they did not travel — until Miriam was gathered — that makes ten, and on the eleventh day they set out from Hazeroth and encamped in the wilderness of Paran, which is Kadesh Barnea, for from there the spies were sent, as written: וילכו ויבאו אל משה ואל אהרן אל מדבר פארן קדשה וגו׳. And the sin caused it, and a decree was issued for the completion of their delay — forty years, as written above: והימים אשר הלכנו מקדש ברנע עד אשר עברנו את נחל זרד שלשים ושמונה שנה עד תום כל הדור וגו׳. And what is written: ונסב את הר שעיר ימים רבים — that was after they set out from Kadesh until they came to Mount Hor, on the border of the land of Edom, in the fortieth year.\nAll this I, the younger [Shemuel ben Meir], have explicated beyond the interpretation in the manuscript of our Master [Rashi], for R. Elazar of Blois set me on the truth. And now I shall return to the interpretation of our Master Shemuel, of blessed memory, and so my teacher instructed me."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Rashbam's comment on this lemma is transmitted in two distinct versions (גירסה א and גירסה ב); both are translated in sequence as they appear in the source.", 1 "The epithet רבינו שמואל refers to Rashi (R. Shlomo Yitzhaki), Rashbam's grandfather; רבי אלעזר מבליינצי is R. Elazar of Blois; הרב at the end likely refers to Rashbam's father, R. Meir."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:38:24.118604563Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}